number  2,  so  the  corresponding  device  should be zstty2, not
zstty1.  The old Zilog 8530 chip has a very small FIFO (3 bytes?)
and therefore has very strict latency requirements for the inter‐
rupt service routine.  This limits the usable baud rates on  many
machines.
